# MAD FIX - the build arm (Mad Check)

The audit finds the dead ends. MAD FIX removes them.

MAD rebuilds a human business owner's website so an AI agent can visit
it and actually purchase the site's products: an agent card
(/.well-known/agent.json), an llms.txt map of the store, a structured
product catalog with one source of truth for prices, an x402 payment
door (USDC on Base) with no card form and no CAPTCHA in the agent
path, and an OpenAPI description of the order endpoints. The human
checkout is untouched - MAD FIX adds a door, it does not rebuild the
store. Optional: an ERC-8004 identity for the business via MAD
Connect.

The build closes with THE MAD TEST run against the finished site
plus a full re-grade. The build is not done until MAD's own test
runs the door end to end. The grade prints either way; nobody is
paid to pass - MAD is paid to build.

Price: 250 USDC one-time per site. 150 USDC when the site already
bought the Agent-Readiness Audit (100 USDC) - the audit's findings
become the build's work order. Re-grade after the owner's own later
changes: 25 USDC. Drift cover after launch: Daily Drift Monitoring
1 USDC/day or 25 USDC/month, or MAD PROTECT 25-150 USDC/month.

Order: mailto:madcheck@proton.me - a filing ID is issued before any
